n:
This section is called The Proverbs of Solomon. It mostly contains short pieces of advice and observations. These sayings often use *antithetical parallelism* to compare wisdom and righteousness with foolishness and wickedness. The proverbs seem to be arranged randomly, similar to Egyptian and Mesopotamian wisdom literature. Some proverbs repeat: 

- {{Proverbs 6:10-11|Proverbs 6:10–11}} and {{Proverbs 24:33-34|24:33–34}}

- {{Proverbs 14:12|Proverbs 14:12}} and {{Proverbs 16:25|16:25}}

- {{Proverbs 18:8|Proverbs 18:8}} and {{Proverbs 26:22|26:22}}

- {{Proverbs 19:24|Proverbs 19:24}} and {{Proverbs 26:15|26:15}}

- {{Proverbs 20:16|Proverbs 20:16}} and {{Proverbs 27:13|27:13}}

- {{Proverbs 21:9|Proverbs 21:9}} and {{Proverbs 25:24|25:24}}

- {{Proverbs 22:3|Proverbs 22:3}} and {{Proverbs 27:12|27:12}}

Sometimes, a group of proverbs shares a similar theme (for example, {{Proverbs 16:1-11|Proverbs 16:1–11}}).
